Your narrative is Claude’s intelligence. Claude is told that Blue has no AWACS or radars, and that Blue must hold St Catherine, win the air over Abu Rudeis, and land a C-130 with an MLRS to hit the missile base. So Abu Rudeis is the key, and stopping the transport matters most.
The C-130 is shot at first. When the bridge launches alert fighters, a detected C-130 goes ahead of any fighter, even a closer one.
The missile base at El Tor is now a defend zone, alongside Abu Rudeis airport and the seaport. Once Red sees an MLRS (or any Blue ground unit) inside one of them, Claude reviews the situation straight away, and Red’s ground-attack jets go after any Blue ground units Red can see near those zones.
